       "about": "how `claude -p` behaves where a stand-in hides it",
       "decided": "A `claude -p` stopped by the usage limit ends, and its reply holds a line with the time the limit resets, such as `You've hit your session limit \u00b7 resets 1:40pm`. Given `--add-dir`, it takes the arguments after it as directories, so the prompt goes on stdin.",
